# Schema-on-write vs schema-on-read

## When do you impose structure?

- **On write** (warehouse) — schema applied **as you load**; ETL conforms data first
- **On read** (lake) — stored **as-is**; structure applied **when you query**

## The trade-off

- On write — **trust & fast reads**, but model up front & rigid
- On read — **flexible & cheap ingest**, but every reader parses; quality varies

## Pairs with ETL vs ELT

- **ETL** — transform → load (schema-on-write)
- **ELT** — load → transform later (schema-on-read; cloud & lakehouse, §08)
